<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  v573: cleartext disabled globally + system trust anchors only.

  CERTIFICATE PINNING WAS CONSIDERED AND REJECTED:
  - We considered pinning bro-api.fly.dev / brix.fly.dev to Let's Encrypt
    roots (ISRG Root X1 + X2). LE roots are valid 9-14 more years.
  - REJECTION REASON: Fly.io controls cert issuance and could switch CA
    at any time. If Fly ever moves away from LE (e.g., to ZeroSSL or
    Cloudflare-issued), pinned builds would BRICK irreparably until
    every user installs a hotfix. Coverage is impossible — some users
    never update.
  - For a payment app, brick risk > marginal MITM protection. We already
    have HTTPS + HSTS + cleartextTrafficPermitted=false. The remaining
    threat (rogue CA in device trust store) requires either targeted
    malware or corporate proxy — both already low probability for our
    Brazilian P2P Bitcoin user base.
  - Future option: Trust-on-First-Use SPKI tracking in custom Dart code
    that warns the user (rather than hard-fails) on certificate change.

  This config remains because:
  1. It locks the application to system trust anchors only (no user
     CAs trusted), blocking custom-CA MITM via Settings > Security
     install. (debug-overrides removed for release.)
  2. Provides a clear hook for future TLS hardening.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="false">
        <trust-anchors>
            <certificates src="system" />
        </trust-anchors>
    </base-config>
</network-security-config>
